Not a horse is absolute perfection.
A horse implies a man with a destination and status; a mule implies a working entertainer whose entire life, equipment, and home are strapped to four legs and an attitude.
The contrast within Curt’s trio completes his little traveling ecosystem:
Parrot: The chaotic, winged smartass perched on his shoulder who speaks only in tavern ditties and loud observations.
The Mule: The unbothered, stubborn anchor who trudges along behind, carrying the heavy juggling gear, camping kit, and wine skins, completely unimpressed by Curt’s charm.
Curt: Walking between them, talking to both like old work buddies.
